# The Held identification branch of Theorem 12.7.7

The source target is an actual isomorphism G ≃ He when C_G(t) is not
contained in M, under the genuine finite simple QTKE hypotheses of §12.7.
The centralizer deduction is proved on the literal closure ⟨Lₜ^{C_G(t)}⟩,
with local structural inputs explicit. The actual component also excludes
M₂₄ once the two marked model kernels are supplied. The component and scalar geometry,
the missing extraspecial construction on printed p.841, and a proved
recognition theorem remain required. No global identification is asserted.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript of 1 March 2004, Theorem 12.7.7, printed pp.840–842 (PDF 857–859).
-/
